# Optional: expose one or more direct Anthropic models in the UI model selector.
# On macOS the server automatically loads the key stored by:
#   ./scripts/setup-anthropic-keychain.sh
TURNTURN_ANTHROPIC_MODELS=replace-with-anthropic-model-id
# Optional overrides:
# TURNTURN_ANTHROPIC_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE=com.turnturn.anthropic-api-key
# TURNTURN_ANTHROPIC_KEYCHAIN_ACCOUNT=your-macos-account
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_HELPER=/absolute/path/to/a-custom-secret-helper

# --- Provider connection, wire adapter, and model (see design.md D30) --------------
#
# These are three separate ideas:
#   - a "provider connection" (e.g. TURNTURN_PROVIDER + TURNTURN_BASE_URL) is which
#     configured account or local runtime receives the request;
#   - a "wire adapter" is which HTTP request/stream grammar is spoken. It is always
#     TURNTURN_PROVIDER's value literally — it is never guessed from a model's name.
#     A LiteLLM connection routing a model named "bedrock-claude-5-sonnet" still
#     speaks openai-chat-completions, not anthropic-messages;
#   - a "model" is just the provider-visible model id string.
#
# The server also discovers additional models per connection at startup and on
# explicit refresh, augmenting (never replacing) the profiles configured above:
#   - TURNTURN_PROVIDER=anthropic-messages (or TURNTURN_ANTHROPIC_MODELS set): lists
#     every model the resolved Anthropic credential can see via GET /v1/models.
#   - TURNTURN_PROVIDER=openai-chat-completions (e.g. a LiteLLM gateway): lists every
#     model TURNTURN_API_KEY can see via the gateway's GET /v1/models. These are
#     LiteLLM routing names, not proof of the upstream model's real wire format.
#   - TURNTURN_PROVIDER=ollama: lists locally installed models via GET /api/tags and
#     checks tool-call capability per model via POST /api/show.
#
# Discovery never blocks startup and never requires credentials beyond what is
# already configured above. One provider being unreachable only marks that
# connection unavailable in the UI's model picker (GET /api/providers); it does not
# remove the models configured above or stop the server from starting.
